      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "We need to compute the expression \\(1 + 6 \\cdot 2 - 3 + 5 \\cdot 4 \\div 2\\). We can break it down step by step following the order of operations, often remembered by the acronym PEMDAS (Parentheses, Exponents, Multiplication and Division (from left to right), Addition and Subtraction (from left to right)).\n\n1. First, perform the multiplication and division from left to right:\n   \\[\n   6 \\cdot 2 = 12\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   5 \\cdot 4 \\div 2 = 5 \\cdot 2 = 10\n   \\]\n   So the expression now is:\n   \\[\n   1 + 12 - 3 + 10\n   \\]\n\n2. Next, perform the addition and subtraction from left to right:\n   \\[\n   1 + 12 = 13\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   13 - 3 = 10\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   10 + 10 = 20\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is \\(\\boxed{20}\\).",
